WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.860
About 1.2 million species
have been catalogued.

2
00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:08.960
Estimates suggest around 8.7
million species of eukaryotes exist.

3
00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:11.150
And everyday names don't help.

4
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.750
A starfish is not a fish.

5
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.470
Say robin in Britain,
then in North America,

6
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.620
and you mean two different birds.

7
00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:23.830
So how can just two words tell you where
any living thing fits among millions?

8
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.580
In this mission, you'll see
why biologists classify at all:

9
00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:31.670
to identify, to predict,
and to trace relationships.

10
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.720
Then you'll learn the rules
for writing a two-part name,

11
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:37.100
from capital letters to italics.

12
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:40.750
Your mission: find out what
each of the two words tells you.
